    <div class="section" id="s1">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Section 01</div>
      <div class="section-title">What is a cyber attack?</div>
      <div class="section-intro">A cyber attack is any deliberate attempt to breach information systems — stealing data,
        disrupting services, or causing damage. Attackers range from lone hackers to organized crime rings to
        nation-state agencies. Just as physical criminals use different tools, cyber attackers have a diverse and
        constantly evolving toolkit.</div>
      <div class="analogy"><strong>Analogy —</strong> Think of the internet as a vast city. Every server is a building.
        Cyber attacks are break-ins: some attackers pick the lock (exploiting vulnerabilities), some forge a key
        (identity spoofing), some trick the receptionist (social engineering), and some blow up the front door (DDoS).
        Each method has a different technique, target, and consequence.</div>

      <!-- Timeline -->
      <div class="diagram-card">
        <div class="diagram-label">Historical timeline of cyber attacks</div>
        <div style="padding:20px 20px 4px;">
          <div class="timeline">
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">1971</div>
              <div class="tl-title">The Creeper — first malware</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">Self-replicating program spread across ARPANET. Displayed "I'm the creeper, catch me
                if you can!" — harmless, but the ancestor of all malware.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">1988</div>
              <div class="tl-title">Morris Worm</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">First major internet worm. Infected ~6,000 machines (10% of the internet) and caused
                up to $100M in damages. Created by Robert Morris at Cornell University.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">2000</div>
              <div class="tl-title">ILOVEYOU virus</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">Philippine-born worm spread via email, infected 10 million computers in 10 days.
                Caused $10B in damage — the first true global cyber epidemic.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">2010</div>
              <div class="tl-title">Stuxnet — cyber warfare begins</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">US-Israeli state-sponsored worm sabotaged Iran's nuclear centrifuges. The first
                cyberweapon to cause real-world physical destruction.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">2017</div>
              <div class="tl-title">WannaCry ransomware</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">Hit 200,000+ computers across 150 countries in 24 hours. Crippled the UK NHS. Caused
                $4–8B in damages using the NSA's EternalBlue exploit.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-item">
              <div class="tl-year">2020</div>
              <div class="tl-title">SolarWinds supply chain attack</div>
              <div class="tl-desc">Russian SVR hackers trojanized a software update, infiltrating ~18,000 organizations
                including US government agencies. One of history's most sophisticated attacks.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
