    <!-- ═══ SECTION 4 — MALWARE ═══ -->
    <div class="section" id="s4">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Section 04</div>
      <div class="section-title">Malware — the digital menagerie</div>
      <div class="section-intro">Malware (malicious software) is an umbrella term for any program designed to harm,
        exploit, or compromise a system. It accounts for over 60% of all cyberattacks and comes in many specialized
        forms.</div>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--red-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
              <path d="M8 12 Q12 6 16 12 Q12 18 8 12Z" fill="#E24B4A" opacity="0.7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Virus</div>
          <div class="card-body">Attaches to legitimate programs. Replicates when the host runs. Can corrupt files or
            serve as a delivery mechanism for other malware. Requires human action to spread.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--red-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <path d="M4 12 C4 6 20 6 20 12 C20 18 4 18 4 12Z" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></path>
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" fill="#E24B4A"></circle>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Worm</div>
          <div class="card-body">Self-replicates without needing a host file. Spreads autonomously across networks
            exploiting vulnerabilities. Far more dangerous than viruses due to speed of propagation.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-crit">Critical</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--amber-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <polygon points="12,3 21,20 3,20" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></polygon>
              <line x1="12" y1="10" x2="12" y2="15" stroke="#BA7517" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
              <circle cx="12" cy="18" r="1" fill="#BA7517"></circle>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Trojan horse</div>
          <div class="card-body">Disguises itself as legitimate software. Once executed, delivers a malicious payload —
            backdoors, data theft, or additional malware downloads. Does NOT self-replicate.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-crit">Critical</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--red-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <rect x="5" y="8" width="14" height="12" rx="2" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></rect>
              <path d="M8 8 V6 A4 4 0 0 1 16 6 V8" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></path>
              <circle cx="12" cy="14" r="2" fill="#E24B4A"></circle>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Ransomware</div>
          <div class="card-body">Encrypts victim's files, demands ransom (usually crypto) for the decryption key. Modern
            variants also exfiltrate data first ("double extortion") for extra leverage.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-crit">Critical</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--amber-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="5" ry="8" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></ellipse>
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2" fill="#BA7517"></circle>
              <path d="M4 12H8M16 12H20" stroke="#BA7517" stroke-width="1"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Spyware</div>
          <div class="card-body">Silently monitors activity — keystrokes, screenshots, webcam, microphone. Sends data to
            attacker. Pegasus spyware (NSO Group) is the most sophisticated known example.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--purple-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="#534AB7" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"></circle>
              <path d="M8 8L16 16M16 8L8 16" stroke="#7F77DD" stroke-width="1.5"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Rootkit</div>
          <div class="card-body">Grants persistent, privileged access while hiding its presence. Operates at OS kernel
            or firmware level. Extremely difficult to detect — often requires full OS reinstall.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-crit">Critical</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--blue-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <rect x="2" y="7" width="6" height="8" rx="1" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"></rect>
              <rect x="9" y="4" width="6" height="11" rx="1" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"></rect>
              <rect x="16" y="7" width="6" height="8" rx="1" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"></rect>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Botnet</div>
          <div class="card-body">A network of compromised computers ("bots") controlled via a C2 server. Used for DDoS
            attacks, spam campaigns, cryptocurrency mining, or large-scale data theft.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-crit">Critical</span>
        </div>
        <div class="atk-card">
          <div class="card-icon-wrap" style="background:var(--gray-bg);">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
              <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="13" rx="2" stroke="#5F5E5A" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"></rect>
              <path d="M7 20H17M12 16V20" stroke="#5F5E5A" stroke-width="1.2"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="card-title">Adware</div>
          <div class="card-body">Displays unwanted ads automatically. Often bundled with free software. Some variants
            cross into spyware behavior, tracking habits and selling data to advertisers.</div>
          <span class="sev sev-med">Medium</span>
        </div>
      </div>

